            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a programme, an event, then the Tamil for a film, a movie."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: தலைக்கவசம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தலைக்கவசம் — talaikkavacam — \"a helmet\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தலைக்கவசம் (talaikkavacam) is native talai, \"head\" (DEDR 3103), and kavacam, \"armour\", from Sanskrit kavaca, \"coat of mail\" (CDIAL 2957), which CDIAL notes may itself be Dravidian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
